\section*{Saturation factor one for even Spin groups}

\subsection{OpenAI's claim}
OpenAI presents a proof in the selected manuscript. For $\operatorname{Spin}(2n)$, $n\geq2$, a tensor invariant at a dilated triple is claimed to imply one at the original triple when the weight sum belongs to the root lattice.

\subsection{Outline of the argument}
The proof constructs reflected weight schedules and resolves the type-D parity obstruction by joining signed-root components. Rank-two reorderings keep the modified schedule admissible, exterior and minuscule column constructions turn it into nonzero intertwiners, and a preprojective-module reduction removes common zero coordinates.

\subsection{Scope relative to this problem}
The main type-D saturation theorem proves equivalence of invariant existence before and after every positive dilation for dominant integral weights with sum in Q(D\_n). The requested implication for some N is one direction of exactly that equivalence. Within these assumptions, this is a claimed affirmative answer to the stated question.

